{"step_index":176,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T08:57:49Z","input_tokens":8525,"cache_read_tokens":245889,"output_tokens":8141,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: creating a second HTML file, named `card_sort_cach_2_canvas_5cols.html`, is the appropriate next step. This file will implement a pixel-based canvas design, featuring cards that dynamically fall and load into five columns. The base card will have the size of 68px.\n\n\nThe canvas will serve as a pixel-based dispenser for the five columns. Pixels from the canvas columns map to the five playable columns. A mechanism is needed to feed pixels to columns, either on demand or when columns drop to a minimal card count, ensuring an \"Empty Column\" option. The mechanics of similar games are considered for a good approach.\n\n\nWhen a column has cards removed, but at least one card remains and the column has fewer than three cards, the canvas automatically feeds a pixel to the top of that column. If a column becomes completely empty, it remains empty, providing an operational choice. If another column is already empty, the empty column pulls two pixels from the canvas. The logic ensures smooth pixel transitions and maintains the operational choice of the empty column.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Playable HTML prototype for Method 2 (card_sort_cach_2_canvas_5cols.html): 10x10 high-resolution Pixel Art Canvas at top feeding pixels down into 5 extra-wide (68px) playable columns below, with dynamic k/Target badges and 1 single-color holding slot.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"vi\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no\">\n  <title>Cách 2: Khung Tranh Pixel 10×10 + 5 Cột Lớn (68px)</title>\n  <style>\n    * {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0